ENUMERATES(2)          ENUMERATES DEFINITION FUNCTIONS            ENUMERATES(2)NAME       enumerates - enumerate variable definitionsSYNOPSIS       #include enumerates.f83       enumerates ( -- )       enum.type ( -- )       enum.null ( -- )       enum ( -- )       >enum ( value -- )       enum.end ( -- )DESCRIPTION       Allows definition of enumerate variable sets.enumerates ( -- )       Vocabulary for enumerate definitions.enum.type ( -- )       Used in the following structure:               enum.type <enum-type-name>                 <enum-items>               enum.end       to start the definition of an enumerate variable and identifiers.        The items start with the value zero. The type may later be used        to define variables:               <enum-type-name> <enum-variable-name>       The variable corresponds to a normal, long, variable.enum.null ( -- )       Used within an "enum.type" definition to advance the item       identification number without defining an item.enum ( -- )       Used within an "enum.type" definition to declare an enumerate.               enum <enum-item-name>       The value of the items are zero and upwards.>enum ( value -- )       Used within an "enum.type" definition to declare an enumerate       symbol with a given value.               <enum-item-value> >enum <enum-item-name>enum.end ( -- )       Ends a "enum.type" definition.SEE ALSO       forth(1)COPYING       Copyright (C) 1989 Mikael R.K. Patel       Permission is granted to make and distribute verbatim copies       of this manual provided the copyright notice and this permission       notice are preserved on all copies.       Permission is granted to copy and distribute modified versions       of this manual under the conditions for verbatim copying,        provided also that the section entitled "GNU General Public       License" is included exactly as in the original, and provided       that the entire result